==Strategy==
It is recommended to only use ranged meat shields such as [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]] so that Kappy's Surge Attacks will miss more often. If you are going to use Cameraman Cat, make sure to bring some Research Up [[Cat Combo]]s. Other ranged units such as [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] or [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]] can really help with damage, and expedite the process.

It is helpful to use fast and cost efficient units such as [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Slime Cat]] or Talented [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]], but they can act as stepping stones for Kappy to spawn a Surge Attack, so be careful. High range crowd-controllers that can outrange Kappy's Surge and Loris' LD, like Talented [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]], [[Asiluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Assassinlan Pasalan]], and [[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Deadeye]] will help make the threats more manageable while staying at a safe distance. If Kappy seems to push too fast and he leaves the blindspot of Cyberpunk, consider using [[Glass Cat (Rare Cat)|Macho Crystal Cat]] and [[Lone Cat and Kitten (Rare Cat)|Tourist Cat]] to push Kappy back.

[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]] is a great unit for this stage due to the removal of Trolly Bloggers who previously would block Stone Cat's path towards Kappy. Stone Cat can stall Kappy in place indefinitely with 3 (Sm) Research Cat Combos. Be mindful to time it so that Stone Cat hits Kappy during his backswing animation, in order to prevent him from using Stone to create a Surge Attack.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*Units with [[Immune to Surge]] like [[Talents|Talented]] [[Boogie Cat (Special Cat)|Gato Amigo]], [[Actress Cat (Special Cat)|Talented Beefcake Cat]] (Lv.50 with max Attack Up and Surge Immune Talents is recommended) and [[Jagando Jr. (Special Cat)|Lord of Ruin Jagando Jr.]] are immensely helpful for chipping away at Kappy, and preventing the loss of ground. For a list of Cats with the "Immune to Surge" ability, see [[:Category:Cats with Surge Immunity|here]].
*[[Classification|Rushers]] such as [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]], and [[Sanada Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Immortal Yukimura]] help out, but make sure to time them so they don't get hit by a Surge Attack. Only use them sparcely, otherwise you might risk bankrupting yourself.

